<div class="article-layout">
<main id="main-content" tabindex="-1"><div class="breadcrumbs"><a href="/guides/">Wiki</a> / <a href="/guides/tf2/">TF2 &amp; Classified</a></div><h1>Troubleshooting</h1><p class="article-intro">Resolve edition selection, loading, missing menu, empty data and script errors.</p><div class="guide-card" id="troubleshooting"><h2 class="sr-only">Troubleshooting</h2><h3>The loader cannot find my game</h3><p>Check Game version first: retail and Classified have different executables. Close duplicate instances of the selected game. Start that edition through the dashboard, or restart it through Steam with <code>-insecure</code>. Wait for the game to reach its menu before retrying.</p><h3>The game changed after an update</h3><p>Use the latest matching TF2 package. The native adapter checks the supported game build and can reject changed modules. Do not substitute files from the other edition; wait for a compatible update when the current build is unsupported.</p><h3>The package is incomplete or fails verification</h3><p>Extract the complete official ZIP again into a fresh folder, keeping its TF2 directory beside the loader. For server downloads, check your connection and retry. Keep your user-data backup; replacing a runtime package does not require deleting profiles.</p><h3>Loaded, but the menu does not appear</h3><p>Focus the game and try Insert or F1. Read the loader’s exact status. If it reports that startup did not accept the session, restart the game and sign in again before retrying. A loaded library alone does not prove that every gameplay feature is active.</p><h3>ESP or Lua queries show no data</h3><p>Enter an eligible local practice/listen-server map and wait for a live local player. Check feature toggles, team/category filters and ranges. In the API, inspect <code>tf2.session()</code>; empty results are expected while disconnected, after Stop or in an ineligible session.</p><h3>A model preview is empty</h3><p>Class-preview models depend on locally generated game assets and are not included in the public runtime ZIPs. A missing preview mesh does not identify a Lua error or an edition mismatch.</p><h3>A script reports an error</h3><p>Open the Lua console, check the named line and function, and compare the example with <a href="/api/tf2/">the TF2 API</a>. Check nil results and API version 1.0. Stop the script, correct it and run it again. Script callbacks and UI are cleaned up when the script is stopped.</p><p>For further help, include your edition, loader message, reproduction steps and the relevant console error. Avoid sharing passwords, keys or session data.</p></div><footer class="wiki-footer"><span>Scooby Wiki · TF2 &amp; Classified</span><div><a href="/products/tf2/">Product page</a><a href="/docs/tf2/">Lua documentation</a><a href="/guides/tf2/">All TF2 guides</a></div></footer></main>
</div>
